course: dictionary
lesson: 2111
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word tells you which meaning to use by the words around it. Those words are the context. «Theo lost three races in a row and threw the controller onto the sofa.» Races, a sofa and throwing point to a game device, so controller means the thing you hold to play.
explain: Other words can change the meaning. An air traffic controller is a person whose job is to guide planes safely. A part of a machine that controls how it works is also called a controller. The words around the word show you which one is meant.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning. If it does not, try the next meaning in your list.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a word with several meanings.
fact: Controller can mean a hand-held device with buttons and sticks, used to play video games or work a machine like a toy car or drone.
fact: Controller can also mean a person whose job is to control or manage something, such as an air traffic controller.
fact: Controller can mean a part of a machine that controls how it works.
fact: «Putting the controller down and walking away for a minute helps the hot feeling pass.» Here controller means the game device.
exercise: «Next time Theo felt the heat rising, he put the controller down and walked to the kitchen for a glass of water first.» What is the controller here? | A glass of water | A person who manages a team | A kitchen table | *A hand-held device for playing games
exercise: An air traffic controller guides planes safely at an airport. What does controller mean in this phrase? | A hand-held device with buttons | *A person whose job is to manage and guide | A part inside a toy car | A type of sofa
exercise: The machine stopped because the controller inside it failed. What does controller mean here? | A person who runs the factory | A game played with friends | *A part of a machine that controls how it works | A remote control for the television
test: «Harrison's little brothers break his PlayStation controller and Dad says, "You should've put it away."» What is the controller in this sentence? | A bag for carrying toys | A part of a bed | *A hand-held device for playing video games | A person in charge of the game
test: Pilots listen to the air traffic controller on the radio. What does controller mean here? | *A person whose job is to manage and guide | A hand-held device with buttons | A toy car | A part of a machine
exam: In «Putting the controller down and walking away for a minute helps the hot feeling pass», what does controller mean? | A person who guides planes | *A hand-held device for playing games | A part of a machine that runs a factory | A sofa cushion
